    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I notice that `cmdheight` is forced to set to 1 when picker window is created, but I have a `cmdheight` of 2. How could I override cmdheight for the picker window?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I notice that <code class=\"notranslate\">cmdheight</code> is forced to set to 1 when picker window is created, but I have a <code class=\"notranslate\">cmdheight</code> of 2. How could I override cmdheight for the picker window?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I notice that cmdheight is forced to set to 1 when picker window is created, but I have a cmdheight of 2. How could I override cmdheight for the picker window?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-07-18T13:45:56Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You can do that by creating an autocommand for [`MiniPickStart`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/db52ea9a1fd5183bb15f557db3fd6e504099bf06/doc/mini-pick.txt#L140) `User` event. Like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal set_cmdheight = function() vim.o.cmdheight = 2 end\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = set_cmdheight })\r\n```\r\n\r\nI thought about altering command line height only if it is zero, but always setting it to 1 seems like a good design because it enforces the biggest  vertical space it can get.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">You can do that by creating an autocommand for <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/db52ea9a1fd5183bb15f557db3fd6e504099bf06/doc/mini-pick.txt#L140\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPickStart</code></a> <code class=\"notranslate\">User</code> event. Like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local set_cmdheight = function() vim.o.cmdheight = 2 end\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = set_cmdheight })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">set_cmdheight</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">o</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">cmdheight</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>MiniPickStart<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">set_cmdheight</span> })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I thought about altering command line height only if it is zero, but always setting it to 1 seems like a good design because it enforces the biggest  vertical space it can get.</p>",
            "bodyText": "You can do that by creating an autocommand for MiniPickStart User event. Like this:\nlocal set_cmdheight = function() vim.o.cmdheight = 2 end\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = set_cmdheight })\nI thought about altering command line height only if it is zero, but always setting it to 1 seems like a good design because it enforces the biggest  vertical space it can get.",
