                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> I think it's very rare that one might set their cmdheight > 3 (right?)\r\n\r\nSure. I'd even go as far as to say that it is not that common to have command height more than 1 :) To be exact, it is 11% of users, [based on the survey](https://gist.github.com/echasnovski/fa70dc75c475369747d2a485a13303fb#file-neovim-survey-summary_02_all-csv). More than I'd guess, though.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think it's very rare that one might set their cmdheight &gt; 3 (right?)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sure. I'd even go as far as to say that it is not that common to have command height more than 1 :) To be exact, it is 11% of users, <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/echasnovski/fa70dc75c475369747d2a485a13303fb#file-neovim-survey-summary_02_all-csv\">based on the survey</a>. More than I'd guess, though.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I think it's very rare that one might set their cmdheight > 3 (right?)\n\nSure. I'd even go as far as to say that it is not that common to have command height more than 1 :) To be exact, it is 11% of users, based on the survey. More than I'd guess, though.",
